{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794254275,"nonce":"E1o1sCmieQmXwYOnPIN7ZP3UCiE=","title":"iOS and Android read system fonts into the heap","message":"The iOS and Android startup paths read each system font path with std::fs::read and hand the bytes to the registry (ios.rs, the system_font_paths loop and blinc_load_bundled_font) or to load_font_data (android.rs). Every byte becomes dirty heap memory. On desktop the default font now loads by path through FontFace::from_file, which memory-maps it; the same on desktop saved 7.9 MB for SFNS.ttf alone.\n\nFix: load these by path (a registry API that hands fontdb the path, so it maps the file) instead of reading them. Measure on a device: the iOS loop loads several system faces.","files":null}]}